.TH NIMDOW 1
.SH NAME
nimdow \- a dynamic tiling window manager for the River Wayland compositor
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B river \-c nimdow
.br
.B nimdow
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B nimdow
.BI \-\-status " TEXT"
.br
.B nimdow
.BR \-\-dumpState " [" \fIFILE\fR ]
.br
.B nimdow
.BI \-\-COMMAND " " \fR[\fIARG\fR]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nimdow
is a dynamic tiling window manager.
It is a window management client of the River Wayland compositor
(version 0.5 or later, using the river-window-management-v1 protocol):
River handles rendering and input devices, nimdow decides how windows are laid out.
Windows are tiled automatically and organized with tags.
Layout and focus are controlled with keybindings from the configuration file,
or via IPC.
nimdow draws its own status bar and provides a system tray
(StatusNotifierItem, with dbusmenu popups).
.
.PP
.B nimdow
also acts as a cli client,
which talks to a running nimdow process via a UNIX socket.
All window manager controls are available via the IPC and cli client.
The UNIX socket is created at
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nimdow/ipc-socket.%p
where %p is the PID of nimdow
(\fB/tmp\fR is used if XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is not set).
.
.PP
Floating windows are supported,
and can be moved/resized with the mouse while holding a modifier key.
.
.SH STARTING
Select the
.B nimdow
session in your login manager
(it runs
.BR "river -c nimdow" ),
or start it from a virtual console with
.BR "river -c nimdow" .
Running
.B nimdow
outside of River does not work.
.
.PP
On startup nimdow imports the display environment (WAYLAND_DISPLAY, XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, ...)
into the systemd user manager and the D-Bus activation environment,
and starts
.BR nimdow-session.target .
That target binds
.B graphical-session.target
and pulls in
.BR xdg-desktop-autostart.target ,
so XDG autostart entries are run.
The target is stopped again when nimdow exits.
Set
.B NIMDOW_NO_SESSION=1
to skip all of this, for example when running nested or in tests.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.
.SS "Generic Commands"
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version \fR
Prints the version information.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fB\-\-config=\fIFILE\fR"
Starts nimdow with the given config file.
.
.SS "Special IPC Commands"
.TP
.BI \-\-status " TEXT"
Sets the text shown in the status bar
(e.g. from a script: \fBnimdow --status "$(date)"\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-dumpState " [" \fIFILE\fR ]
Makes the running instance write its state (monitors, tags, windows, bar, menus) as JSON.
Meant for debugging, bug reports and tests.
.TP
.BR \-\-exitSession
Exits nimdow (River exits with it).
.
.SS "IPC Commands"
.
.TP
.BR --reload-config
Reloads all settings from your config file.
.
.TP
.BR --increase-master-count
Increases the number of master windows in the layout.
.
.TP
.BR --decrease-master-count
Decreases the number of master windows in the layout.
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-to-previous-monitor
Moves the selected window to the previous monitor.
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-to-next-monitor
Moves the selected window to the next monitor.
.TP
.BR --focus-previous-monitor
Focuses the previous monitor (wraps around to the last monitor).
.
.TP
.BR --focus-next-monitor
Focuses the next monitor (wraps around to the first monitor).
.
.TP
\fB--go-to-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
Views the selected tag.
.
.TP
.BR --go-to-left-tag
Goes to the tag on the left.
.
.TP
.BR --go-to-right-tag
Goes to the tag on the right.
.
.TP
.BR --go-to-previous-tag
Views the previously viewed tag.
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-to-previous-tag
Moves the selected window to the previously viewed tag.
.
.TP
\fB--toggle-tag-view\fR \fITAG\fR
Toggles the visibility of a tag.
.
.TP
\fB--toggle-window-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
Toggles the assignment of a window to a tag.
.
.TP
.BR --focus-previous
Focuses the previous window.
.
.TP
.BR --focus-next
Focuses the next window.
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-previous
Moves the window to the previous position in the window stack.
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-next
Moves the window to the next position in the window stack.
.
.TP
\fB--move-window-to-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
Moves the selected window to the tag associated with the given number.
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-to-left-tag
Moves the window to the tag on the left.
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-to-right-tag
Moves the window to the tag on the right.
.
.TP
.BR --toggle-fullscreen
Toggles the fullscreen state of the selected window.
.
.TP
.BR --destroy-selected-window
Destroys the selected window.
.
.TP
.BR --toggle-floating
Toggles the floating state of the selected window.
.
.TP
.BR --jump-to-urgent-window
Finds and selects the first urgent window.
.
.TP
.BR --increase-master-width
Increases the width of the master window.
.
.TP
.BR --decrease-master-width
Decreases the width of the master window.
.
.TP
.BR --rotate-clients
Rotate clients clockwise, making the last window master
.
.TP
.BR --move-window-to-scratchpad
Moves the selected window to the scratchpad.
.
.TP
.BR --pop-scratchpad
Brings back the window most recently added to the scratchpad.
.
.TP
.BR --toggle-statusbar
Hides or shows the status bar on the selected monitor.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nimdow/config.toml
The configuration file (\fB~/.config/nimdow/config.toml\fR by default).
If it does not exist,
.B /usr/share/nimdow/config.default.toml
is used.
.TP
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nimdow/ipc-socket.PID
The IPC socket.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/systemd/user/nimdow-session.target
The systemd user target started with the session.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NIMDOW_NO_SESSION
If set to a non-empty value, nimdow does not touch the systemd user session
(no environment import, no
.BR nimdow-session.target ).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory of the IPC socket.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the user configuration.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR river (1),
.BR systemd.special (7)
